configure — ISSUE FOUND
JavaScript distinguishes an omitted property from a present undefined property.

Input
  base        { retries: 0 }
  override    {  }

JavaScript representation
  base        { retries: 0 }
  override    { retries: <present undefined> }

Result
  verified    RetryConfig.RetryConfig(Option.Some(0))
  JavaScript  { retries: <present undefined> } (exactly RetryConfig.RetryConfig(Option.None))

Cause
  The formal optional value is absent in both cases, but JavaScript object spread and property presence can observe the difference.

Resolve
  Canonicalize optional records at the boundary, or extend the formal representation to track property presence.

